{"base_rate":0.32982917214191854,"brier":0.14762601839684625,"bss":0.3321355565971409,"bss_hi":0.46502833541485467,"bss_lo":0.17109737461596985,"chart":{"base":[347.1,154.4],"fp":[173.0,138.6],"lead":"62,249.2 272,222.6 482,204 692,156","note":{"base":"skill 0.33 — higher than 62% of cities","fp":"low end -3pp, high end +26pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 47% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 0%; promised 96% → rained 72%"},"rel":"80.4,464.6 358.3,379.6 666.4,156.4"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16155059132720104,"ess":411.5249822115553,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Fukuoka</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Fukuoka rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 4.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.33, ranked 83 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(30&ndash;161) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>226</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>236</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Fukuoka</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;33% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 33% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.33</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>30&ndash;161\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Fukuoka &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Fukuoka\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.97115044247788,377.16814159292034 95.39692307692307,316.6666666666667 172.07184210526316,228.61710526315855 278.34108108108114,116.37837837837839 356.95549295774646,48.76056338028167 409.85499999999996,18.0 409.85499999999996,24.169491525423723 356.95549295774646,105.28309859154928 278.34108108108114,195.0810810810811 172.07184210526316,300.57894736842104 95.39692307692307,368.0 58.97115044247788,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"261.9421813403417\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"261.9421813403417\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.97115044247788,382.0 95.39692307692307,377.3333333333333 172.07184210526316,329.3157894736842 278.34108108108114,288.5405405405405 356.95549295774646,253.83098591549296 409.85499999999996,81.23728813559319\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 226 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.97115044247788\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"95.39692307692307\" cy=\"377.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"172.07184210526316\" cy=\"329.3157894736842\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"278.34108108108114\" cy=\"288.5405405405405\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"356.95549295774646\" cy=\"253.83098591549296\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 236 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.85499999999996\" cy=\"81.23728813559319\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(33%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Fukuoka the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.55) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.05).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>-0.050</td><td class='num'>30.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.391</td><td class='num'>16.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.431</td><td class='num'>12.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.555</td><td class='num'>5.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":33.6,"lon":130.41667,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Fukuoka","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.002743362831858407,"n":226,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.19,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.10564102564102562,"n":78,"obs":0.01282051282051282,"sig":true},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.19,"mean":0.32223684210526315,"n":76,"obs":0.14473684210526316,"sig":true},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.6224324324324325,"n":74,"obs":0.25675675675675674,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.75,"mean":0.8445070422535211,"n":71,"obs":0.352112676056338,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9939406779661016,"n":236,"obs":0.826271186440678,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.4,"provisional":false,"rank":83,"rank_hi":161.0,"rank_lo":30.0,"reliability":0.048373415247667,"resolution":0.12302480972940327,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"fukuoka","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo"}